---
import { getProductsWithPricing } from "../../lib/bookeo";
import Article from "../../layouts/article.astro";

const { data, info } = await getProductsWithPricing();
if (!data) {
  throw new Error(`No data found`);
}
if (info.totalPages > 1) {
  throw new Error("Pagination not implemented");
}
---

<Article
  showLanguageSwitcher={false}
  title="Book a guided tour"
  description="Book a tour in Paris, from tours in Montmartre to personalised tours"
>
  <h1>Book a guided tour with me</h1>
  <p>
    Hi, I'm Abi and I'm a tour guide in Paris. Here you can find the different
    tours that I offer. You can learn more about me <a href="/articles/about/"
      >here</a
    >!
  </p>
  <p>
    I host private tours, so they are personalised to your needs! This means
    that I can adjust the start time and location of the tours, find suitable
    activities that are perfect for your group and be there to guide you through
    the city!
  </p>
  <p>
    I currently offer two types of walking tours, the first being a tour that is
    in a specific area, and the other type is completely personalised based on
    what you're looking for. This can be close to where you're staying, or can
    be an area you'd just like to explore.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every guide has their own style, and for me, that style is not reciting from
    a book, but rather through telling stories, asking and answering questions
    and sharing the Paris experience.
  </p>
  <p>
    My tours are not just about the places we are walking through, they're also
    about giving you the best experience for your trip. I'm happy to answer
    questions about the city and give advice on what other activities you can
    plan.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you would like to book a tour and you don't find what you're looking for,
    you can get in contact via <a href="mailto:contact@abisummers.com"
      >contact@abisummers.com</a
    >.
  </p>
  <br />

  <h2>Available tours</h2>

  <style>
    .products {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1em;
    }
    .product {
      max-width: 100%;
      width: 100%;
      border: 0.1em solid currentColor;
      padding: 0.5em;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5em;
    }
    .product img {
      display: block;
      max-width: calc(100% + 1em);
      width: calc(100% + 1em);
      margin: -0.5em;
      height: auto;
      aspect-ratio: 2/1;
      object-fit: cover;
    }
    .product .cta {
      align-self: flex-end;
    }

    .product .row {
      display: flex;
      gap: 1em;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
    }
  </style>

  <style is:global>
    .product p {
      margin: 0;
    }
  </style>

  <div class="products">
    {
      data.map((entry) => (
        <article class="product">
          <img src={entry.images[0].url} width={448} height={252} alt="" />
          <div class="row">
            <a href={`/book/${entry.productCode}/`}>
              <h3>{entry.name}</h3>
            </a>
            <p>
              {[
                { time: entry.duration.days, unit: "days" },
                { time: entry.duration.hours, unit: "hours" },
                { time: entry.duration.minutes, unit: "minutes" },
              ]
                .filter((segment) => segment.time)
                .map((segment) => `${segment.time} ${segment.unit}`)
                .join(", ")}
            </p>
            {entry.basePrice ? <p>{entry.basePrice.amount} €</p> : undefined}
          </div>
          <Fragment set:html={entry.description} />
          <a class="cta" href={`/book/${entry.productCode}/`}>
            Book
          </a>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p>
    If you don't find what you're looking for, don't hesitate to reach out to me
    via <a href="mailto:contact@abisummers.com">contact@abisummers.com</a> with some
    information about what you'd like to see and do. This might to be to explore a
    specific area (eg Le Marais or close to where you're staying), where to get the
    best street food, or how to plan a trip with children.
  </p>
  <p>
    Paris has so much to offer, and I love getting to show people the version of
    Paris they're wanting to explore.
  </p>
</Article>
